        "original_id": "6d098ecd-0fe5-5610-8c1c-8f49ca3d1279",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Koyaanisqatsi, Mad Hot Ballroom, Powaqqatsi\n- People: Godfrey Reggio, Philip Glass, Ron Fricke, Marilyn Agrelo, Amy Sewell\n- Organizations: New York City Department of Education\n- Concepts: experimental film, documentary film, sequel\n\nFacts:\n- Koyaanisqatsi, also known as Koyaanisqatsi: Life Out of Balance, is a 1982 American experimental film directed by Godfrey Reggio, with music by Philip Glass and cinematography by Ron Fricke.\n- Powaqqatsi, also known as Powaqqatsi: Life in Transformation, is a 1988 American documentary film directed by Godfrey Reggio and a sequel to his 1982 experimental film Koyaanisqatsi.\n- Mad Hot Ballroom is a 2005 American documentary film directed and co-produced by Marilyn Agrelo and written and co-produced by Amy Sewell.\n- Mad Hot Ballroom is about a ballroom dance program for fifth graders in the New York City Department of Education, the New York City public school system.",
